WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.841
Imagine one score list where first place

00:00:02.861 --> 00:00:05.058
barely beats second, and another where

00:00:05.078 --> 00:00:07.570
first place wins by a huge margin.

00:00:07.745 --> 00:00:10.753
Both order the records A, B, C.

00:00:10.915 --> 00:00:13.692
Would reciprocal rank fusion notice how

00:00:13.712 --> 00:00:15.238
different those gaps were?

00:00:15.413 --> 00:00:16.591
Pause and predict.

00:00:18.998 --> 00:00:20.999
It would not. Once the scores become

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:23.396
ranks, those gaps disappear from the

00:00:23.416 --> 00:00:26.463
fusion input. Our score sets are invented

00:00:26.483 --> 00:00:29.955
illustrations. RRF preserves position and

00:00:29.975 --> 00:00:32.520
record identity, not the strength of the

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.607
original numerical separation.

00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:37.488
The constant changes how much a high

00:00:37.508 --> 00:00:38.905
position is worth.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.019
With constant zero, first place

00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:43.957
contributes one and third contributes one

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.470
third. With constant sixty, the

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:49.266
contributions are one over sixty one and

00:00:49.286 --> 00:00:52.410
one over sixty three: much closer.

00:00:52.931 --> 00:00:55.025
This changes the balance between very high

00:00:55.045 --> 00:00:57.924
positions and agreement across lists.

00:00:58.086 --> 00:01:00.373
That baseline constant can be tuned for a

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.506
different task.

00:01:01.668 --> 00:01:03.929
It does not set the number of retrieved or

00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:05.321
displayed records.

00:01:06.226 --> 00:01:08.602
Cut each supplied list from three records

00:01:08.622 --> 00:01:12.648
to two. The lexical list becomes A, B; the

00:01:12.668 --> 00:01:15.457
dense list becomes C, A.

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:17.777
C loses its lexical third place

00:01:17.797 --> 00:01:20.123
contribution, while D disappears from the

00:01:20.143 --> 00:01:22.764
supplied candidate pool altogether.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.194
That is different from fusing the original

00:01:25.214 --> 00:01:28.686
four identities and displaying just A and

00:01:28.706 --> 00:01:31.805
C. In the latter case, B and D had fused

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:34.833
scores but fell below the output boundary.

00:01:35.008 --> 00:01:37.964
Input cutoffs change what fusion receives.

00:01:38.864 --> 00:01:41.905
The baseline gives every supplied list

00:01:41.925 --> 00:01:44.082
equal weight. An implementation can

00:01:44.102 --> 00:01:47.240
instead multiply each list’s contributions

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.708
by an explicit weight.

00:01:48.845 --> 00:01:50.435
In a declared extension of the same

00:01:50.455 --> 00:01:53.683
example, give dense contributions twice

00:01:53.703 --> 00:01:56.234
the weight of lexical contributions.

00:01:56.787 --> 00:01:58.986
C then narrowly overtakes A.

00:01:59.148 --> 00:02:01.924
The arithmetic is reproducible, but the

00:02:01.944 --> 00:02:04.064
weighting choice is not a quality

00:02:04.084 --> 00:02:05.120
recommendation.

00:02:05.269 --> 00:02:07.028
The hybrid label leaves those weighting

00:02:07.048 --> 00:02:09.115
choices unspecified.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:12.326
The chapter describes Web of Science Smart

00:02:12.346 --> 00:02:14.955
Search document search combining a Boolean

00:02:14.975 --> 00:02:18.008
keyword path and a semantic vector path.

00:02:18.183 --> 00:02:20.534
A parser first structures the query;

00:02:20.658 --> 00:02:22.764
combining the retrieval paths makes it

00:02:22.784 --> 00:02:23.524
hybrid.

00:02:24.089 --> 00:02:27.149
Scopus AI can choose lexical retrieval,

00:02:27.311 --> 00:02:30.087
vector retrieval, or both per question.

00:02:30.262 --> 00:02:33.168
A one path run combines nothing under the

00:02:33.188 --> 00:02:34.275
book’s definition.

00:02:34.463 --> 00:02:37.072
When both paths run, their results still

00:02:37.092 --> 00:02:38.721
need a fusion rule.

00:02:38.871 --> 00:02:41.144
These are pinned documentation accounts,

00:02:41.164 --> 00:02:42.871
not new service tests.

00:02:43.773 --> 00:02:45.956
With a blend, the prescribed evidence

00:02:45.976 --> 00:02:48.456
sources give the explanation a fixed

00:02:48.476 --> 00:02:50.969
shape. With routing, the answer to was

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:53.830
this lexical or vector search can change

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.247
from query to query.

00:02:55.409 --> 00:02:57.413
Expose the routing choice before

00:02:57.433 --> 00:02:58.662
explaining a result.

00:02:59.222 --> 00:03:01.864
A rule, classifier or model can choose

00:03:01.884 --> 00:03:04.943
routes. Routing alone does not establish

00:03:04.963 --> 00:03:08.913
agency. Nor does naming RRF identify the

00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:11.413
candidate architecture: the same fusion

00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:13.603
formula can combine lists produced by

00:03:13.623 --> 00:03:14.878
other arrangements.

00:03:15.774 --> 00:03:18.744
Elsevier’s twenty twenty four Scopus AI

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:21.747
RAG Fusion account describes generated

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.151
query variants.

00:03:23.326 --> 00:03:26.450
Vector retrieval runs for each variant,

00:03:26.638 --> 00:03:29.208
and reciprocal rank fusion merges their

00:03:29.228 --> 00:03:31.889
result lists before top results support a

00:03:31.909 --> 00:03:34.672
summary with references for claims.

00:03:35.198 --> 00:03:37.292
This account concerns multiple variant

00:03:37.312 --> 00:03:40.101
lists, rather than lexical and dense lists

00:03:40.121 --> 00:03:42.807
for one query. Its presence establishes

00:03:42.827 --> 00:03:45.410
neither different retrieval methods nor a

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.665
later version’s route choices.

00:03:48.577 --> 00:03:51.996
Use RRF as a baseline and compare it with

00:03:52.016 --> 00:03:53.606
the individual retrievers on

00:03:53.626 --> 00:03:55.075
representative queries.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.859
Document the routes, candidate depths,

00:03:57.879 --> 00:04:00.526
duplicate identity handling, constant,

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:03.477
weights, output cutoff and any later

00:04:03.497 --> 00:04:07.305
reranker. Evaluate the actual task, rather

00:04:07.325 --> 00:04:08.554
than the hybrid label.

00:04:09.088 --> 00:04:11.087
The result depends on which evidence

00:04:11.107 --> 00:04:13.393
survives each choice.

00:04:13.556 --> 00:04:16.383
Rank fusion avoids incompatible score

00:04:16.403 --> 00:04:19.476
scales by discarding score gaps; routing

00:04:19.496 --> 00:04:21.885
decides which lists can contribute at all.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.780
Chapter Eleven follows query

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.860
interpretation, transformation and routing

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.097
in more detail.
